  <https://orca-graph.example/ontology/> rdfs:comment """
        An ontology for the collaborative authoring of scopes, hierarchical
        components and key performance indicators.
    """@en,
      """
        Ontología para la creación colaborativa de ámbitos, componentes
        jerárquicos e indicadores clave de rendimiento.
    """@es .
  
  orca:SupportAgent rdfs:comment """
        An agent that supports a value-chain link. A KPI applies directly to
        this agent rather than to the link.
    """@en,
      "Son aquellos que fortalecen la cadena mediante conocimiento, financiación, regulación, coordinación o promoción, pero sin intervenir directamente en las operaciones productivas. Ejemplos: Administraciones públicas, Universidades y centros de formación, Centros tecnológicos y de investigación, Asociaciones sectoriales, Cámaras de comercio, Entidades financieras, Organismos de certificación."@es .
  
  orca:KPI rdfs:comment """
        A key performance indicator used to evaluate performance against
        a defined objective.
    """@en,
      "Indicadores cuantitativos o cualitativos que permiten medir o valorar el rendimiento de una actividad o proceso en relación con los objetivos establecidos, facilitando la toma de decisiones y la mejora continua."@es .
  
  orca:ValueChainLink rdfs:comment """
        A stage, activity or link that forms part of a value chain.
    """@en,
      "Cada una de las etapas o conjuntos de actividades que forman parte del proceso de creación, transformación y entrega de valor de un producto o servicio, desde el origen de las materias primas hasta el consumidor final."@es .
  
  orca:hasAssociatedKPI rdfs:comment """
        Relates an agent of any type to a KPI associated with that agent.
    """@en,
      """
        Relaciona un agente de cualquier tipo con un KPI asociado a dicho
        agente.
    """@es .
  
  orca:Agent rdfs:comment """
        An actor that participates in one or more links of a value chain.
    """@en,
      "Cualquier organización, empresa, institución o individuo que participa, de forma directa o indirecta, en alguna de las etapas de la cadena de valor y contribuye a la creación, transformación, distribución o comercialización de un producto o servicio."@es .
  
  orca:appliesToAgent rdfs:comment """
        Relates a KPI directly to an agent, regardless of whether the agent is
        principal, auxiliary or support.
    """@en,
      """
        Relaciona un KPI directamente con un agente, con independencia de que
        sea principal, auxiliar o de apoyo.
    """@es .
  
  orca:hasParticipatingAgent rdfs:comment """
        Relates a value-chain link to any participating agent.
    """@en,
      """
        Relaciona un eslabón de la cadena de valor con cualquier agente que
        participa en él.
    """@es .
  
  orca:AuxiliaryAgent rdfs:comment """
        An agent that participates in a value-chain link in an auxiliary
        capacity. A KPI applies directly to this agent rather than to the link.
    """@en,
      "Son aquellos que proporcionan bienes o servicios necesarios para el funcionamiento operativo de la cadena, contribuyendo de forma directa a que las actividades productivas, de transformación o comercialización puedan desarrollarse, sin tomar posesión del producto en su tránsito por la cadena."@es .
  
  orca:participatesInValueChainLink rdfs:comment """
        Relates any agent to a value-chain link in which it participates.
    """@en,
      """
        Relaciona cualquier agente con un eslabón de la cadena de valor en el
        que participa.
    """@es .
  
  orca:hasPrincipalAgent rdfs:comment """
        Relates a value-chain link to one of its principal agents.
    """@en,
      """
        Relaciona un eslabón de la cadena de valor con uno de sus agentes
        principales.
    """@es .
  
  orca:PrincipalAgent rdfs:comment """
        An agent whose main activity belongs to one or more value-chain links.
        KPIs apply directly to the agent.
    """@en,
      "Agente que ejecuta directamente alguna de las actividades centrales de creación, transformación o comercialización del producto pesquero —captura/extracción, procesado, distribución o venta— tomando posesión del producto en esa fase y haciéndolo avanzar hacia el consumidor final. Por su posición en el flujo del producto, ejerce una influencia estratégica sobre la generación de valor y el funcionamiento del conjunto de la cadena."@es .
  
  orca:belongsTo rdfs:comment """
        Relates a principal agent to the value-chain link to which its main
        activity belongs.
    """@en,
      """
        Relaciona un agente principal con el eslabón de la cadena de valor
        al que pertenece su actividad principal.
    """@es .
  
  orca:isComponentOf rdfs:comment """
        Relates a component to a scope that groups it.
    """@en,
      """
        Relaciona un componente con un ámbito que lo agrupa.
    """@es .
  
  orca:Component rdfs:comment """
        A thematic component grouped by a scope. A component can contain
        multiple subcomponents and can have associated KPIs.
    """@en,
      "Aspectos específicos que se analizan dentro de cada ámbito temático que permite área concreta de estudio de la cadena de valor"@es .
  
  orca:Scope rdfs:comment """
        A thematic area that groups zero or more components. Scopes are not
        arranged hierarchically and do not relate directly to KPIs.
    """@en,
      "Áreas temáticas desde las cuales se analiza una cadena de valor para comprender su organización, competitividad, sostenibilidad, capacidad de innovación y contribución al desarrollo económico y social."@es .
  
  orca:hasComponent rdfs:comment """
        Relates a scope to one of the components that it groups.
    """@en,
      """
        Relaciona un ámbito con uno de los componentes que agrupa.
    """@es .
  
  orca:appliesToComponent rdfs:comment "Relates a KPI directly to the component to which it applies."@en,
      "Relaciona un KPI directamente con el componente al que se aplica."@es .
  
  orca:hasKPI rdfs:comment "Relates a component to a KPI that applies to it."@en, "Relaciona un componente con un KPI que se aplica a él."@es .
  
  orca:description rdfs:comment """
        A textual description of a scope, component, KPI, agent, value chain
        or value-chain link.
    """@en,
      """
        Descripción textual de un ámbito, componente, KPI, agente, cadena de
        valor o eslabón.
    """@es .
  
  orca:ValueChain rdfs:comment """
        An ordered or structured set of links through which value is created.
    """@en,
      "Conjunto de actividades y agentes que intervienen desde la captura o extracción de los recursos pesqueros hasta el consumo final de los alimentos, aportando valor en cada etapa mediante procesos de captura, producción, transformación, distribución y comercialización."@es .
  
  orca:hasSubcomponent rdfs:comment "Relates a component to one of its direct subcomponents."@en,
      "Relaciona un componente con uno de sus subcomponentes directos."@es .
  
  orca:similarTo rdfs:comment """
        Relates two scopes or two KPIs that are considered semantically
        similar. The relation is symmetric but not transitive.
    """@en,
      """
        Relaciona dos ámbitos o dos KPI que se consideran semánticamente
        similares. La relación es simétrica, pero no transitiva.
    """@es .
  
  orca:hasValueChainLink rdfs:comment "Relates a value chain to one of its constituent links."@en,
      """
        Relaciona una cadena de valor con uno de sus eslabones.
    """@es .
  
  orca:isValueChainLinkOf rdfs:comment "Relates a value-chain link to its value chain."@en,
      """
        Relaciona un eslabón de cadena de valor con la cadena a la que
        pertenece.
    """@es .
  
  orca:name rdfs:comment "The name of a scope, component or KPI."@en, "Nombre de un ámbito, componente o KPI."@es .
}

<https://orca-graph.example/graph/ontology/om-2.0> {
  :Unit rdfs:comment "A unit of measure is a definite magnitude of a quantity, defined and adopted by convention or by law. It is used as a standard for measurement of the same quantity, where any other value of the quantity can be expressed as a simple multiple of the unit. For example, length is a quantity; the metre is a unit of length that represents a definite predetermined length. When we say 10 metre (or 10 m), we actually mean 10 times the definite predetermined length called \"metre\"."@en,
      "測定単位とは，量の確定的な大きさであり，慣例又は法律によって定義し採用されている。同じ量の測定の標準として用いられ，他の如何なる量の値も当該単位の単純な倍数として表わせる。例えば，長さも量である; メートルは長さの単位であり，確定的な所定の長さを表している。10メートル（又は10 m）とは，「メートル」と呼ばれる確定的な所定の長さの10倍を，実際に意味している。"@ja .
  
  :unofficialLabel rdfs:comment "Used to specify labels that are used in e.g. every day speech but are not defined in any standard." .
  
  :unofficialAbbreviation rdfs:comment "Used to specify abbreviations that are used in e.g. every day speech but are not defined in any standard." .
  
  :Quantity rdfs:comment "A quantity is a representation of a quantifiable (standardised) aspect (such as length, mass, and time) of a phenomenon (e.g., a star, a molecule, or a food product). Quantities are classified according to similarity in their (implicit) metrological aspect, e.g. the length of my table and the length of my chair are both classified as length."@en,
      "量とは，ある現象（例: 星・分子・食品）の定量化できる（標準化された）性質（例: 長さ・質量・時間）の表現である。量は（暗黙の）計量的類似性に従って分離される。例: 机の長さ及び椅子の長さは双方とも長さに分類される。"@ja .
  
  :Measure rdfs:comment "A measure combines a number to a unit of measure. For example, \"3 m\" is a measure."@en .
  
  :Point rdfs:comment "A point is an element of an interval scale or a ratio scale, for example, 273.16 on the Kelvin scale indicates the triple point of water thermodynamic temperature."@en .
  
  :commonlyHasUnit rdfs:comment "This property indicates a commonly-used unit." .
  
  :Prefix rdfs:comment "A prefix is a name that precedes a basic unit of measure to indicate a decimal or binary multiple or fraction of the unit. Each prefix has a unique symbol that is prepended to the unit symbol. For example, an electric current of 0.000 000 001 ampere is written by using the SI-prefix nano as 1 nanoampere or 1 nA."@en .
  
  :ApplicationArea rdfs:comment "An application area groups quantities and units of measure for application areas such as scientific disciplines (e.g., thermodynamics, mechanics)."@en .
  
  :Dimension rdfs:comment "Dimensions are abstract properties of units and quantities neglecting their vectorial or tensorial character and all numerical factors including their sign."@en .
  
  :SystemOfUnits rdfs:comment "In order to achieve a coherent, interdependent set of units of measure in the wide variety of units that exist, units are organised in systems of units. A system of units is based on a set of units chosen by convention to be the system’s base units, units that are considered to be mutually independent (i.e., can’t be expressed in terms of each other)."@en .
  
  :LaTeXCommand rdfs:comment "OMLaTeX command that can be used to render this quantity or unit."@en .
  
  :LaTeXSymbol rdfs:comment "OMLaTeX formatted symbol may include commands such as \\unit and \\E as defined in OMLaTeX."@en .
  
  :alternativeLaTeXSymbol rdfs:comment "An alternative OMLaTeX formatted symbol, which may include commands such as \\unit and \\E as defined in OMLaTeX."@en .
  
  :Length rdfs:comment "Length is the amount of space between two geographical points along a curve. It is a base quantity in the International System of Units and other systems of units. Length is speed times time. The metre, a base unit of length in the International System of Units, is defined in terms of speed of light during a certain time interval."@en .
  
  :Area rdfs:comment "Area expresses the two-dimensional size of a defined part of a surface, typically a region bounded by a closed curve. It is a derived quantity in the International System of Units. Area is length squared."@en .
  
  :Volume rdfs:comment "Volume is a measure of how much three-dimensional space any phenomenon occupies. It is a derived quantity in the International System of Units. Volume is length to the power 3."@en .
  
  :Angle rdfs:comment "Angle is the ratio between an arc and its radius."@en .
  
  :SolidAngle rdfs:comment "Solid angle is the ratio of the surface of a portion of a sphere enclosed by the conical surface that forms an angle to the square of the radius of the sphere."@en .
  
  :chain rdfs:comment "The chain is a unit of length defined as 20.1168 metre."@en .
  
  :cicero rdfs:comment "The cicero is a unit of length defined as 12 point (Didot)."@en .
  
  :fathom-USSurvey rdfs:comment "The US survey fathom is a unit of length defined as 1.828804 metre."@en .
  
  :fermi rdfs:comment "The fermi is a unit of length defined as 1.0e-15 metre."@en .
  
  :foot-International rdfs:comment "The international foot is a unit of length defined as 3.048e-1 metre."@en .
  
  :foot-USSurvey rdfs:comment "The US survey foot is a unit of length defined as 3.048006e-1 metre."@en .
  
  :furlong-International rdfs:comment "The international furlong is a unit of length defined as 201.168 metre."@en .
  
  :inch-International rdfs:comment "The international inch is a unit of length defined as 2.54e-2 metre."@en .
  
  :metre rdfs:comment "The metre is a unit of length defined as the length of the path travelled by light in vacuum during a time interval of 1/299 792 458 of a second."@en .
  
  :micrometre rdfs:comment "The micrometre is a unit of length defined as 1.0e-6 metre."@en .
  
  :millimetre rdfs:comment "The millimetre is a unit of length defined as 1.0e-3 metre."@en .
  
  :centimetre rdfs:comment "The centimetre is a unit of length defined as 1.0e-2 metre."@en .
  
  :decimetre rdfs:comment "The decimetre is a unit of length defined as 1.0e-1 metre."@en .
  
  :decametre rdfs:comment "The decametre is a unit of length defined as 1.0e1 metre."@en .
  
  :hectometre rdfs:comment "The hectometre is a unit of length defined as 1.0e2 metre."@en .
  
  :kilometre rdfs:comment "The kilometre is a unit of length defined as 1.0e3 metre."@en .
  
  :megametre rdfs:comment "The megametre is a unit of length defined as 1.0e6 metre."@en .
  
  :gigametre rdfs:comment "The gigametre is a unit of length defined as 1.0e9 metre."@en .
  
  :micron rdfs:comment "The micron is a unit of length defined as 1.0e-6 metre."@en .
  
  :mil-Length rdfs:comment "The mil (length) is a unit of length defined as 2.54e-5 metre."@en .
  
  :mile-Statute rdfs:comment "The statute mile is a unit of length defined as 1.609344e3 metre."@en .
  
  :mile-USSurvey rdfs:comment "The US survey mile is a unit of length defined as 1.609347e3 metre."@en .
  
  :nauticalMile-International rdfs:comment "The international nautical mile is a unit of length defined as 1852 metre."@en .
  
  :pica-ATA rdfs:comment "The ATA pica is a unit of length defined as 12 point (ATA)."@en .
  
  :pica-Postscript rdfs:comment "The Postscript pica is a unit of length defined as 12 point (Postscript)."@en .
  
  :pica-TeX rdfs:comment "The TeX pica is a unit of length defined as 12 point (TeX)."@en .
  
  :point-ATA rdfs:comment "The ATA point is a unit of length defined as 0.3514598e-3 metre."@en .
  
  :point-Didot rdfs:comment "The Didot point is a unit of length defined as 0.3759e-3 metre."@en .
  
  :point-Postscript rdfs:comment "The Postscript point is a unit of length defined as 0.013888888888888888888888888888889 inch."@en .
  
  :point-TeX rdfs:comment "The TeX point is a unit of length defined as 0.01383700013837000138370001383 inch."@en .
  
  :rod-US rdfs:comment "The US rod is a unit of length defined as 5.029210 metre."@en .
  
  :yard-International rdfs:comment "The international yard is a unit of length defined as 9.144e-1 metre."@en .
  
  :angstrom rdfs:comment "The angstrom is a unit of length defined as 1.0e-10 metre. The unit is often used for wavelengths of electromagnetic radiation or to express the sizes of atoms and molecules."@en .
  
  :attometre rdfs:comment "The attometre is a unit of length defined as 1.0e-18 metre."@en .
  
  :femtometre rdfs:comment "The femtometre is a unit of length defined as 1.0e-15 metre."@en .
  
  :picometre rdfs:comment "The picometre is a unit of length defined as 1.0e-12 metre."@en .
  
  :nanometre rdfs:comment "The nanometre is a unit of length defined as 1.0e-9 metre."@en .
  
  :astronomicalUnit rdfs:comment "The atronomical unit is a unit of length defined as 149 597 870 700 metre (IAU 2012 Resolution)."@en .
  
  :lightYear rdfs:comment "The light year is a unit of length defined as 9.46073e15 metre."@en .
  
  :terametre rdfs:comment "The terametre is a unit of length defined as 1.0e12 metre."@en .
  
  :petametre rdfs:comment "The petametre is a unit of length defined as 1.0e15 metre."@en .
  
  :exametre rdfs:comment "The exametre is a unit of length defined as 1.0e18 metre."@en .
  
  :parsec rdfs:comment "The parsec is a unit of length defined as 3.08567758149137e16 metre."@en .
  
  :megaparsec rdfs:comment "The megaparsec is a unit of length defined as 1.0e6 parsec. Gebruikt voor afstanden op de schaal van clusters."@en .
  
  :acre-International rdfs:comment "The international acre is a unit of area defined as 4.0468564224e3 square metre."@en .
  
  :acre-USSurvey rdfs:comment "The US survey acre is a unit of area defined as 4.046872609874252e3 square metre."@en .
  
  :are rdfs:comment "The are is a unit of area defined as 100 square metre."@en .
  
  :barn rdfs:comment "The barn is a unit of area defined as 1.0e-28 square metre."@en .
  
  :centiare rdfs:comment "The centiare is a unit of area defined as 1.0e-2 are."@en .
  
  :circularMil rdfs:comment "The cicular mil is a unit of area defined as 5.067075e-10 square metre."@en .
  
  :hectare rdfs:comment "The hectare is a unit of area defined as 1.0e2 are."@en .
  
  :squareMetre rdfs:comment "Square metre is a unit of area defined as the area of a square whose sides measure exactly one metre."@en .
  
  :acreFoot rdfs:comment "The acre foot is a unit of volume defined as 1.233489e3 cubic metre."@en .
  
  :barrel-US rdfs:comment "The US barrel is a unit of volume defined as 1.589873e-1 cubic metre."@en .
  
  :bushel-US rdfs:comment "The US bushel is a unit of volume defined as 3.523907e-2 cubic metre."@en .
  
  :cord rdfs:comment "The cord is a unit of volume defined as 3.624556 cubic metre."@en .
  
  :cubicMetre rdfs:comment "Cubic metre is a unit of volume defined as the volume of a cube whose sides measure exactly one metre."@en .
  
  :cup-USCustomary rdfs:comment "The US customary cup is a unit of volume defined as 2.365882e-4 cubic metre."@en .
  
  :dryGallon-US rdfs:comment "The US dry gallon is a unit of volume defined as 4.40488377086e-3 cubic metre."@en .
  
  :dryPint-US rdfs:comment "The US dry pint is a unit of volume defined as 5.506105e-4 cubic metre."@en .
  
  :dryQuart-US rdfs:comment "The US dry quart is a unit of volume defined as 1.101221e-3 cubic metre."@en .
  
  :fluidOunce-Imperial rdfs:comment "The imperial fluid ounce is a unit of volume defined as 2.841306e-5 cubic metre."@en .
  
  :fluidOunce-US rdfs:comment "The US fluid ounce is a unit of volume defined as 2.957353e-5 cubic metre."@en .
  
  :gallon-Imperial rdfs:comment "The imperial gallon is a unit of volume defined as 4.54609e-3 cubic metre."@en .
  
  :gallon-US rdfs:comment "The US gallon is a unit of volume defined as 3.785412e-3 cubic metre."@en .
  
  :gill-Imperial rdfs:comment "The imperial gill is a unit of volume defined as 1.420653e-4 cubic metre."@en .
  
  :gill-US rdfs:comment "The US gill is a unit of volume defined as 1.182941e-4 cubic metre."@en .
  
  :litre rdfs:comment "The litre is a unit of volume defined as 1.0e-3 cubic metre."@en .
  
  :liquidPint-US rdfs:comment "The US liquid pint is a unit of volume defined as 4.731765e-4 cubic metre."@en .
  
  :liquidQuart-US rdfs:comment "The US liquid quart is a unit of volume defined as 9.463529e-4 cubic metre."@en .
  
  :peck-US rdfs:comment "The US peck is a unit of volume defined as 8.809768e-3 cubic metre."@en .
  
  :pint-Imperial rdfs:comment "The pint is a unit of volume defined as 568.26125 millilitre."@en .
  
  :quart-Imperial rdfs:comment "The imperial quart is a unit of volume defined as 1.1365 litre."@en .
  
  :stere rdfs:comment "The stere is a unit of volume defined as cubic metre."@en .
  
  :tablespoon-US rdfs:comment "The US tablespoon is a unit of volume defined as 1.478676e-5 cubic metre."@en .
  
  :teaspoon-US rdfs:comment "The US teaspoon is a unit of volume defined as 4.928922e-6 cubic metre."@en .
  
  :dessertspoon rdfs:comment "The desserspoon is a unit of volume defined as 2 teaspoon."@en .
  
  :ton-Register rdfs:comment "The register ton is a unit of volume defined as 100 cubic foot = 2.8316846592 cubic metre."@en .
  
  :degree rdfs:comment "The degree is a unit of angle defined as 1.745329e-2 radian."@en .
  
  :gon rdfs:comment "The gon is a unit of angle defined as 1.570796e-2 radian."@en .
  
  :mil-Angle rdfs:comment "The mil (angle) is a unit of angle defined as 9.817477e-4 radian."@en .
  
  :minute-Angle rdfs:comment "The minute (angle) is a unit of angle defined as 2.908882e-4 radian."@en .
  
  :radian rdfs:comment "The radian is a unit of angle defined as the angle subtended at the center of a circle by an arc that is equal in length to the radius of the circle."@en .
  
  :revolution rdfs:comment "The revolution is a unit of angle defined as 6.283185 radian."@en .
  
  :second-Angle rdfs:comment "The second (angle) is a unit of angle defined as 4.848137e-6 radian."@en .
  
  :millisecond-Angle rdfs:comment "The millisecond (angle) is a unit of length defined as 1.0e-3 second (angle). Used in astronomy (measurements of positions of stars, galaxies, etc.) to represent the error."@en .
  
  :microsecond-Angle rdfs:comment "The microsecond (angle) is a unit of length defined as 1.0e-6 second (angle). Used in astronomy (measurements of positions of stars, galaxies, etc.) to represent the error."@en .
  
  :steradian rdfs:comment "The steradian is a unit of solid angle defined as the solid angle subtended at the center of a sphere by a portion of the surface of the sphere that has an area equal to the square of the radius of the sphere."@en .
  
  :solarRadius rdfs:comment "Solar radius is a unit used in astronomy to denote stellar or stellar system radii (http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/solarRadius)."@en .
  
  :gigaparsec rdfs:comment "The gigaparsec is a unit of length defined as 1.0e9 parsec. Gebruikt voor de afstand op de schaal van het heelal."@en .
  
  :kiloparsec rdfs:comment "The kiloparsec is a unit of length defined as 1.0e3 parsec. Gebruikt voor afstanden op de schaal van het melkwegstelsel."@en .
  
  :yoctometre rdfs:comment "The yoctometre is a unit of length defined as 1.0e-24 metre."@en .
  
  :zeptometre rdfs:comment "The zeptometre is a unit of length defined as 1.0e-21 metre."@en .
  
  :zettametre rdfs:comment "The zettametre is a unit of length defined as 1.0e21 metre."@en .
  
  :yottametre rdfs:comment "The yottametre is a unit of length defined as 1.0e24 metre."@en .
  
  :Mass rdfs:comment "Mass is the amount of matter of a phenomenon. It is a base quantity in the International System of Units. Mass is force divided by acceleration."@en .
  
  :Time rdfs:comment "Time is a base quantity in the International System of Units and other systems of units. It is measured by numbers of repetitions of cyclical events."@en .
  
  :Frequency rdfs:comment "Frequency is a measure of the number of occurrences of a repeating event per unit time."@en .
  
  :Force rdfs:comment "Force is the extent to which an object with mass can be caused to accelerate. It is a derived quantity in the International System of Units. Force is mass times acceleration."@en .
  
  :Energy rdfs:comment "Energy can be defined as the ability to do work. It is a derived quantity in the International System of Units."@en .
  
  :Pressure rdfs:comment "Pressure is the force applied to or distributed over a surface. It is a derived quantity in the International System of Units. Pressure is force divided by area."@en .
  
  :DynamicViscosity rdfs:comment "Viscosity is the definite resistance to change of form of many materials."@en .
  
  :KinematicViscosity rdfs:comment "Kinematic viscosity is the ratio of viscosity to density."@en .
  
  :Luminance rdfs:comment "Luminous flux is the total visible energy emitted by a source per unit time."@en .
  
  :Illuminance rdfs:comment "Illuminance is the total luminous flux incident on a surface per unit area."@en .
  
  :gram rdfs:comment "The gram is a unit of mass defined as 1.0e-3 kilogram."@en .
  
  :second-Time rdfs:comment "The second is a unit of time defined as the duration of 9 192 631 770 periods of the radiation corresponding to the transition between the two hyperfine levels of the ground state of the cesium 133 atom."@en .
  
  :hertz rdfs:comment "The hertz is a unit of frequency defined as 1 divided by second."@en .
  
  :dyne rdfs:comment "The dyne is a unit of force defined as 1.0e-5 newton."@en .
  
  :erg rdfs:comment "The erg is a unit of energy defined as 1.0e-7 joule."@en .
  
  :microbar rdfs:comment "The microbar is a unit of pressure defined as 1.0e-6 bar."@en .
  
  :poise rdfs:comment "The poise is a unit of dynamic viscosity defined as 1.0e-1 pascal second (time)."@en .
  
  :stokes rdfs:comment "The stokes is a unit of kinematic viscosity defined as 1.0e-4 square metre per second (time)."@en .
  
  :gal rdfs:comment "The gal is a unit of acceleration defined as centimetre per second (time) squared."@en .
  
  :stilb rdfs:comment "The stilb is a unit of luminance defined as 1.0e4 candela per square metre."@en .
  
  :phot rdfs:comment "The phot is a unit of illuminance defined as 1.0e4 lux."@en .
  
  :ElectricCurrent rdfs:comment "Electric current is the flow of electric charge. It is a base quantity in the International System of Units. Electric current is electric charge divided by time."@en .
  
  :ElectricCharge rdfs:comment "Electric charge is a conserved property of some subatomic particles, which determines their electromagnetic interaction. It is a derived quantity in the International System of Units. Electric charge is electric current times time."@en .
  
  :Capacitance rdfs:comment "Capacitance is the ability to hold electrical charge. It is a derived quantity in the International System of Units. Capacitance is electric charge divided by electric potential."@en .
  
  :Inductance rdfs:comment "Inductance is that property in an electrical circuit where a change in the current flowing through that circuit induces an electromotive force that opposes the change in current."@en .
  
  :ElectricalConductance rdfs:comment "Electrical conductance is a measure of how easily electricity flows along a certain path through an electrical element."@en .
  
  :ElectricalResistance rdfs:comment "Electrical resistance is the degree to which an object opposes an electric current through it. It is a derived quantity in the International System of Units.  Electrical resistance is electric potential divided by electric current."@en .
  
  :ElectricPotential rdfs:comment "Electric potential is the potential energy per unit charge associated with static (time-invariant) electric field."@en .
  
  :MagneticFlux rdfs:comment "Magnetic flux through any area perpendicular to a magnetic field is the product of the area by the field strength."@en .
  
  :abampere rdfs:comment "The abampere is a unit of electric current defined as 10 ampere."@en .
  
  :abcoulomb rdfs:comment "The abcoulomb is a unit of electric charge defined as 10 coulomb."@en .
  
  :abfarad rdfs:comment "The abfarad is a unit of capacitance defined as 1.0e9 farad."@en .
  
  :abhenry rdfs:comment "The abhenry is a unit of inductance defined as 1.0e-9 henry."@en .
  
  :abmho rdfs:comment "The abmho is a unit of electrical conductance defined as 1.0e9 siemens."@en .
  
  :abohm rdfs:comment "The abohm is a unit of electrical resistance defined as 1.0e-9 ohm."@en .
  
  :abvolt rdfs:comment "The abvolt is a unit of electric potential defined as 1.0e-8 volt."@en .
  
  :oersted rdfs:comment "The oersted is a unit of magnetic field defined as 7.957747e1 ampere per metre."@en .
  
  :gauss rdfs:comment "The gauss is a unit of magnetic flux density defined as 1.0e-4 tesla."@en .
  
  :maxwell rdfs:comment "The maxwell is a unit of magnetic flux defined as 1.0e-8 weber."@en .
  
  :gilbert rdfs:comment "The gilbert is a unit of electric current defined as 7.957747e-1 ampere."@en .
  
  :statcoulomb rdfs:comment "The statcoulomb is a unit of electric charge defined as 3.335641e-10 coulomb."@en .
  
  :statampere rdfs:comment "The statampere is a unit of electric current defined as 3.335641e-10 ampere."@en .
  
  :statvolt rdfs:comment "The statvolt is a unit of electric potential defined as 2.997925e2 volt."@en .
  
  :stattesla rdfs:comment "The stattesla is a unit of magnetic flux density defined as 2.9979e6 tesla."@en .
  
  :statfarad rdfs:comment "The statfarad is a unit of capacitance defined as 1.112650e-12 farad."@en .
  
  :stathenry rdfs:comment "The stathenry is a unit of inductance defined as 8.987552e11 henry."@en .
  
  :statmho rdfs:comment "The statmho is a unit of electrical conductance defined as 1.112650e-12 siemens."@en .
  
  :statohm rdfs:comment "The statohm is a unit of electrical resistance defined as 8.987552e11 ohm."@en .
  
  :statweber rdfs:comment "The statweber is a unit of magnetic flux defined as 2.9979e2 weber."@en .
  
  :biot rdfs:comment "The biot is a unit of electric current defined as 10 ampere."@en .
  
  :franklin rdfs:comment "The franklin is a unit of electric charge defined as 3.335641e-10 coulomb."@en .
  
  :ThermodynamicTemperature rdfs:comment "Thermodynamic temperature is the absolute measure of temperature. Its zero point is the temperature at which the particle constituents of matter have minimal motion and can be no colder. Thermodynamic temperature is a base quantity in the International System of Units."@en .
  
  :AmountOfSubstance rdfs:comment "Amount of substance is the number of elementary entities such as atoms, molecules, electrons, particles, etc. present in a phenomenon. It is a base quantity in the International System of Units."@en .
  
  :LuminousIntensity rdfs:comment "Luminous intensity is the wavelength-weighted power emitted by a light source in a particular direction per unit solid angle. It is a base quantity in the International System of Units. Luminous intensity is luminous flux divided by solid angle."@en .
  
  :Speed rdfs:comment "Speed is the time rate of motion measured by the distance moved over in unit time."@en .
  
  :Momentum rdfs:comment "Momentum is the product of mass and velocity of an object."@en .
  
  :Wavenumber rdfs:comment "Wavenumber is the number of repeating units of a propagating wave (the number of times a wave has the same phase) per unit of space."@en .
  
  :Density rdfs:comment "Density is the concentration of matter. It is a derived quantity in the International System of Units. Density is mass divided by volume."@en .
  
  :SpecificVolume rdfs:comment "Specific volume is volume per unit mass."@en .
  
  :Power rdfs:comment "Power is the time rate at which work is done. It is a derived quantity in the International System of Units. Power is energy divided by time."@en .
  
  :Torque rdfs:comment "Torque is the effectiveness of a force to produce rotation about an axis, measured by the product of the force and the perpendicular distance from the line of action of the force to the axis."@en .
  
  :SurfaceTension rdfs:comment "Surface tension is an attractive property of the surface of a liquid."@en .
  
  :Irradiance rdfs:comment "Irradiance is the power of electromagnetic radiation at a surface per unit area."@en .
  
  :HeatCapacity rdfs:comment "Heat capacity is the heat required to increase the temperature of a system or substance one unit temperature."@en .
  
  :CurrentDensity rdfs:comment "Current density is the density of flow of a conserved charge. It is a derived quantity in the International System of Units. Current density is electric current divided by area."@en .
  
  :LuminousFlux rdfs:comment "Luminous flux is the total visible energy emitted by a source per unit time."@en .
  
  :AbsorbedDose rdfs:comment "Absorbed dose is the energy deposited in a medium by ionizing radiation. It is a derived quantity in the International System of Units. Absorbed dose is energy divided by mass."@en .
  
  :DoseEquivalent rdfs:comment "Dose equivalent is a measure of the radiation dose to tissue where an attempt has been made to allow for the different relative biological effects of different types of ionizing radiation."@en .
  
  :Activity rdfs:comment "Activity is the decay rate of a radioactive substance. It is a derived quantity in the International System of Units. Activity is 1 divided by time."@en .
  
  :kilogram rdfs:comment "The kilogram is a unit of mass defined as the mass of the international prototype of the kilogram."@en .
  
  :ampere rdfs:comment "The ampere is a unit of electric current defined as the constant current that produces an attractive force of 2e–7 newton per metre of length between two straight, parallel conductors of infinite length and negligible circular cross section placed one metre apart in a vacuum."@en .
  
  :kelvin rdfs:comment "The kelvin is a unit of temperature defined as 1/273.16 of the thermodynamic temperature of the triple point of water."@en .
  
  :mole rdfs:comment "The mole is a unit of amount of substance defined as the amount of substance of a system that contains as many elementary entities as there are atoms in 0.012 kilogram of carbon 12."@en .
  
  :candela rdfs:comment "The candela is a unit of luminous intensity defined as the luminous intensity, in a given direction, of a source that emits monochromatic radiation of frequency 540e12 hertz and that has a radiant intensity in that direction of 1/683 watt per steradian."@en .
  
  :metrePerSecond-Time rdfs:comment "Metre per second is a unit of speed defined as metre divided by second."@en .
  
  :metrePerSecond-TimeSquared rdfs:comment "Metre per second squared is a unit of acceleration defined as metre divided by second squared."@en .
  
  :reciprocalMetre rdfs:comment "Reciprocal metre is a unit of wavenumber defined as 1 divided by metre."@en .
  
  :kilogramPerCubicmetre rdfs:comment "Kilogram per cubic metre is a unit of density defined as kilogram divided by cubic metre."@en .
  
  :gramPerCubicmetre rdfs:comment "Gram per cubic metre is a unit of density defined as gram divided by cubic metre."@en .
  
  :milligramPerCubicmetre rdfs:comment "Milligram per cubic metre is a unit of density defined as milligram divided by cubic metre."@en .
  
  :gramPerCubicCentimetre rdfs:comment "Gram per cubic centimetre is a unit of density defined as gram divided by cubic centimetre."@en .
  
  :microgramPerCubicCentimetre rdfs:comment "Microram per cubic centimetre is a unit of density defined as microgram divided by cubic centimetre."@en .
  
  :kilogramPerCubicDecimetre rdfs:comment "Kilogram per cubic decimetre is a unit of density defined as kilogram divided by cubic decimetre."@en .
  
  :cubicMetrePerKilogram rdfs:comment "Cubic metre per kilogram is a unit of specific volume defined as cubic metre divided by kilogram."@en .
  
  :litrePerKilogram rdfs:comment "Litre per kilogram is a unit of specific volume defined as litre divided by kilogram."@en .
  
  :amperePerSquareMetre rdfs:comment "Ampere per square metre is a unit of current density defined as ampere divided by square metre."@en .
  
  :amperePerMetre rdfs:comment "Ampere per metre is a unit of magnetic field defined as ampere divided by metre."@en .
  
  :molePerCubicmetre rdfs:comment "Mole per cubic metre is a unit of amount of substance concentration defined as mole divided by cubic metre."@en .
  
  :candelaPerSquareMetre rdfs:comment "Candela per square metre is a unit of luminance defined as candela divided by square metre."@en .
  
  :newton rdfs:comment "The newton is a unit of force defined as kilogram timesmetre divided by second squared."@en .
  
  :pascal rdfs:comment "The pascal is a unit of pressure and stress defined as newton divided by square metre = joule divided by cubic metre = kilogram divided by metre second squared."@en .
  
  :joule rdfs:comment "The joule is a unit of energy defined as kilogram times square metre divided by second squared."@en .
  
  :watt rdfs:comment "The watt is a unit of power defined as joule divided by second = newton times metre divided by second = volt times ampere = kilogram times square metre divided by second to the power 3."@en .
  
  :coulomb rdfs:comment "The coulomb is a unit of electric charge defined as ampere times second = farad times volt."@en .
  
  :volt rdfs:comment "The volt is a unit of electric potential defined as watt divided by ampere = joule divided by coulomb = newton times metre divided by ampere times second = kilogram times square metre divided by ampere times second to the power 3."@en .
  
  :farad rdfs:comment "The farad is a unit of capacitance defined as ampere times second divided by volt = coulomb divided by volt = coulomb squared divided by joule = coulomb squared divided by newton times metre = second squared times coulomb squared divided by square metre times kilogram = second to the power 4 times ampere squared divided by square metre times kilogram."@en .
  
  :ohm rdfs:comment "The ohm is a unit of electrical resistance defined as volt divided by ampere = square metre times kilogram divided by second to the power 3 times ampere squared."@en .
  
  :siemens rdfs:comment "The siemens is a unit of electrical conductance defined as 1 divided by ohm = ampere divided by volt = coulomb squared times second divided by kilogram times square metre = ampere squared times second to the power 3 divided by kilogram times square metre."@en .
  
  :weber rdfs:comment "The weber is a unit of magnetic flux defined as kilogram times square metre divided by second squared times ampere = volt times second = joule divided by ampere."@en .
  
  :tesla rdfs:comment "The tesla is a unit of magnetic flux density defined as volt times second divided by square metre = newton divided by ampere times metre = weber divided by square metre = kilogram divided by coulomb times second = kilogram divided by ampere times second squared."@en .
  
  :henry rdfs:comment "The henry is a unit of inductance defined as square metre times kilogram divided by second squared times ampere squared = weber divided by ampere = volt second divided by ampere = (joule divided by coulomb) times second divided by (coulomb divided by second) = joule times second squared divided by coulomb squared = square metre times kilogram divided by coulomb squared."@en .
  
  :degreeCelsius rdfs:comment "The degree Celsius is a unit of temperature defined as 1 kelvin."@en .
  
  :lumen rdfs:comment "The lumen is a unit of luminous flux defined as candela times steradian = lux times square metre."@en .
  
  :lux rdfs:comment "The lux is a unit of illuminance defined as lumen divided by square metre = candela times steradian divided by square metre."@en .
  
  :becquerel rdfs:comment "The becquerel is a unit of activity defined as the activity of a quantity of radioactive material in which one nucleus decays per second. Algebraically it is defined as 1 divided by second."@en .
  
  :gray rdfs:comment "The gray is a unit of absorbed dose defined as joule divided by kilogram = square metre divided by second squared."@en .
  
  :sievert rdfs:comment "The sievert is a unit of dose equivalent defined as joule divided by kilogram = square metre divided by second squared."@en .
  
  :katal rdfs:comment "The katal is a unit of catalytic activity defined as mole divided by second."@en .
  
  :yoctogram rdfs:comment "The yoctogram is a unit of mass defined as 1.0e-24 gram."@en .
  
  :zeptogram rdfs:comment "The zeptgram is a unit of mass defined as 1.0e-21 gram."@en .
  
  :attogram rdfs:comment "The attogram is a unit of mass defined as 1.0e-18 gram."@en .
  
  :picogram rdfs:comment "The picogram is a unit of mass defined as 1.0e-12 gram."@en .
  
  :femtogram rdfs:comment "The femtogram is a unit of mass defined as 1.0e-15 gram."@en .
  
  :nanogram rdfs:comment "The nanogram is a unit of mass defined as 1.0e-9 gram."@en .
  
  :microgram rdfs:comment "The microgram is a unit of mass defined as 1.0e-6 gram."@en .
  
  :milligram rdfs:comment "The milligram is a unit of mass defined as 1.0e-3 gram."@en .
  
  :centigram rdfs:comment "The centigram is a unit of mass defined as 1.0e-2 gram."@en .
  
